        "subject": "feat(console): an invited administrator sets up their own password and authenticator (0115)",
        "body": "feat(console): an invited administrator sets up their own password and authenticator (0115)\n\n/admin/setup, for an administrator invited on the server: the address,\nthe one-time setup code passed on privately, and a password of their own\n(12+ characters, typed twice). The API answers with a 30-minute enrolment\ntoken for this browser only; the page signs in with the new password and\nopens the existing enrolment at once with that token, then the recovery\ncodes, shown once. Nothing administrative opens before the authenticator\nis confirmed.\n\nEvery refusal is one localized sentence (EN/FR/AR) that never says whether\nan address, a code or an account exists; a throttled try says so in the\npage's words. Field problems are said beside their fields before anything\nis sent. The code, the password and the token are not kept on the page.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n",
        "author": {
          "name": "CLAUDE",
          "email": "abdelkerim.mahfoudh@gmail.com",
